  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1258 PM CDT Wed Sep 30 2026\n\nWith the front stalled across Deep South Texas, there will be\ncontinuing chances for rain into the weekend. The excessive PW\nvalues will have moved out of our CWA and rainfall totals will be\nmore moderate. A few showers may linger into Monday. By Tuesday\nthe front will have moved away and upper level ridging will move\nback over Texas bringing dry weather back. With cloudy skies and\nscattered showers the long term period will start off cooler with\nhighs in the 70s and 80s Saturday. From there temperatures will\nslowly increase reaching the low to mid 80s by Tuesday.",
